30,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found that we lose an hour daily to copying records, and misrouted deliveries happen because different units have different addresses for the same firm. It's... a lot of waste.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,May,,"Oh boy, we have a problem. The coordination group is understaffed, and our only two developers are busy until the third quarter. We can't just wish for more people!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"As I suspected, the groundwork is shaky. Customer plants have terrible signal half the time, and getting devices approved takes forever. Vendor queries are also a repetitive mess.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The capital budget is frozen, though we have some room in the software allowance. Also, per-head licenses are getting more expensive, while fixed-fee work remains stable.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"This is interesting! Tools that required everyone to enter data daily were dropped, but narrow tools for one trade survived. Most cross-unit efforts just ended without an owner.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, if the developers are busy, does that mean we can't build anything new right now?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, exactly! Unless we use a vendor, but @Ryuji, didn't you say something about license costs?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, your finding about ""owners"" is key. If a project is too broad, it just dies. We need something specific and manageable.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, yes. Per-head licenses climb with every department. If we want something sustainable, a fixed-fee build is much safer for the budget.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, I agree! We need a tool that doesn't rely on a massive, coordinated effort from everyone, or it'll just be dropped like the last ones.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I just... I feel like we should fix the address and copying issues. It's where the real frustration is for the staff.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, I agree, but we have to be realistic about the rota. We can't add more manual work to the coordination group; they're already drowning.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, if the capital budget is frozen, we should avoid anything requiring new hardware or expensive site-specific setups. The network issues at plants make me very nervous.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, I concur. We must prioritize the software allowance and avoid escalating license fees. A project with a fixed cost is the only rational choice.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"So we need something that solves a specific problem, doesn't need a huge team to maintain, and fits the software budget. That sounds like a plan!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
