55,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Looking at these, the Supplier Data Hub solves the address and copying problems I found. It seems like it would help the people on the floor the most.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,May,,"The Workflow Assistant sounds helpful, but the Supplier Data Hub is a central repository. If it's a fixed-fee build, it won't break the staff rota.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"I'm immediately ruling out the Field Service App. With the network coverage and approval delays I found, it would be a disaster in the field.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,The Training Studio might be too expensive if it requires new equipment. The Supplier Data Hub fits the software allowance and addresses a clear inefficiency.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"The Supplier Data Hub is like a catalogue. My research showed that narrow, useful resources survive, while broad ""everyone-must-use-it"" tools fail. This fits!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, do you think the Data Hub would add too much work for the coordination group?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, as long as it's a central hub and not a daily manual entry task for everyone, it should be fine. It actually reduces the repetitive queries Shunichi mentioned.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, if we go with the Hub, can we ensure it's a fixed-fee project? I don't want to see the costs spiral as we add units.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, that is the most prudent approach. Given the frozen capital budget, a fixed-fee software implementation for the Hub is the most stable path.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Kenji,,I'm totally on board with the Supplier Data Hub! It's a tangible resource that solves a real problem without being an over-ambitious failure.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I feel confident about the Supplier Data Hub. It's the most compassionate choice for the people struggling with the records.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,May,,I agree. It solves the vendor query mess and doesn't require our missing developers to do everything from scratch if we use a vendor.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"It avoids the ""field"" risks and the ""broad-scale"" failure risks. It's the only logical choice that doesn't ignore the technical reality.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,It aligns with the software allowance and avoids the capital freeze. I see no reason to choose any other candidate.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"It's a winner! It's a specific tool, it's useful, and it's sustainable. I'm ready to vote.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
